{"title":"Gauge","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>Gauge</b> is a more accurate way to 'measure' a partition that its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Partition\">norm</a>.\n</p><p>A Gauge is essentially a strictly positive function defined on an interval. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gauge&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A funcion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06f3bfaeb41926ee6a1165d3fa1863b35ce1f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> is said to be a <b>Gauge</b> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0711cd8a707dc07303b0c5bc2e0a6164baf955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta(x)&gt;0\\forall x\\in[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval\" title=\"Partition of an interval\">tagged partition</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7e611d201b87739261e63095fdc63b6e0ca6fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}=\\{([x_{i-1},x_i],t_i)\\}_{i=1}^n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" /> is said to be <i><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a42a8b725c200085e5253db2d2fbf8dab898a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta$\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />-fine</i> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea6ec504d6ed3dfed294b42d9e222742483ad4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x_{i-1},x_i]\\subset(t_i-\\delta(t_i),t_i+\\delta(t_i))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>The statement that a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a42a8b725c200085e5253db2d2fbf8dab898a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta$\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />-fine partition exists for evey gauge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a42a8b725c200085e5253db2d2fbf8dab898a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta$\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is true, but is not trivial.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gauge&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Henstock-Kurzweil_integral\" title=\"Henstock-Kurzweil integral\">Henstock-Kurzweil integral</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Continuity\" title=\"Continuity\">Continuity</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Gauge&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085330\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 59/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 256/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1642/500